  <h2>1. Executive Summary & Project Objective</h2>
  <p>
    The objective of this assignment is to design, implement, and deploy a comprehensive web-based <strong>Array Operations Simulator & Memory Address Visualizer</strong>. The application enables students, educators, and developers to interactively explore fundamental computer science memory models and array operations.
  </p>
  <p>Key learning outcomes and software capabilities implemented include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1D & 2D Memory Address Calculations:</strong> Row-Major Order (RMO) and Column-Major Order (CMO) mapping with customizable Base Address, Element Size, Matrix Dimensions, and 0-Based / 1-Based indexing bounds.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive Data Structure Operations:</strong> Step-by-step visual animation for Array Insertion, Deletion, Linear Search ($O(N)$), and Binary Search ($O(\log N)$).</li>
    <li><strong>Hardware Physical DRAM Module Visualizer:</strong> Byte-level RAM representation displaying actual hex addresses (`0x03E8` to `0x03FF`) and blocked memory boundaries.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive Matrix Grid:</strong> Clickable cell-grid interface enabling instant selection and mathematical recalculation.</li>
    <li><strong>Modern UI/UX Design:</strong> iOS-inspired 3D Liquid Crystal Glassmorphism styling with 4 theme presets (Liquid Crystal, Cyberpunk Neon, Midnight Obsidian, Light Frost Glass).</li>
  </ul>

