  <h2>3. Mathematical Foundations & Memory Formulas</h2>

  <h3>3.1 One-Dimensional (1D) Array Address Formula</h3>
  <p>For a 1D array with Base Address $B$, Element Size in Bytes $W$, Target Index $i$, and Lower Bound $L$ (0 or 1):</p>
  <div class="formula-box">
    Address(A[i]) = BaseAddress + W × (i - L)
  </div>

  <h3>3.2 Two-Dimensional (2D) Row-Major Order (RMO) Formula</h3>
  <p>In Row-Major Order, elements are stored row by row sequentially in memory. For a matrix of size $M \times N$ (Rows × Columns):</p>
  <div class="formula-box">
    Address(A[i][j]) = BaseAddress + W × [ (i - L_r) × N + (j - L_c) ]
  </div>
  <p>where $L_r$ is row lower bound, $L_c$ is column lower bound, and $N$ is total columns.</p>

  <h3>3.3 Two-Dimensional (2D) Column-Major Order (CMO) Formula</h3>
  <p>In Column-Major Order, elements are stored column by column sequentially in memory:</p>
  <div class="formula-box">
    Address(A[i][j]) = BaseAddress + W × [ (j - L_c) × M + (i - L_r) ]
  </div>
  <p>where $M$ is total rows.</p>

  <h2>4. Algorithm Analysis & Pseudocode Specification</h2>

  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Operation</th>
        <th>Time Complexity</th>
        <th>Space Complexity</th>
        <th>Pseudocode Implementation</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Address Calculation</strong></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><pre style="margin:0;">Offset = (i * N + j) * W;&#10;Address = BaseAddress + Offset;</pre></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Insertion</strong></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(N)</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><pre style="margin:0;">for (i = N; i > targetIndex; i--)&#10;    A[i] = A[i - 1];&#10;A[targetIndex] = newValue;</pre></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Deletion</strong></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(N)</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><pre style="margin:0;">for (i = targetIndex; i < N - 1; i++)&#10;    A[i] = A[i + 1];&#10;N = N - 1;</pre></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Linear Search</strong></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(N)</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><pre style="margin:0;">for (i = 0; i < N; i++)&#10;    if (A[i] == target) return i;&#10;return -1;</pre></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Binary Search</strong></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(log N)</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge">O(1)</span></td>
        <td><pre style="margin:0;">while (low <= high) {&#10;    mid = floor((low + high) / 2);&#10;    if (A[mid] == target) return mid;&#10;    else if (A[mid] < target) low = mid + 1;&#10;    else high = mid - 1;&#10;}</pre></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>5. Test Cases & Verification Results</h2>

  <h3>Test Case 1: 2D Row-Major Order Memory Calculation</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Base Address = `1000`, Element Size = `4` bytes, Rows = `4`, Cols = `4`, Target Row = `2`, Target Col = `3`, Indexing = `0-Based`.</li>
    <li><strong>Calculation:</strong> $\text{Offset} = [(2 - 0) \times 4 + (3 - 0)] \times 4 = [8 + 3] \times 4 = 11 \times 4 = 44$ bytes.</li>
    <li><strong>Result Address (Decimal):</strong> `1044`</li>
    <li><strong>Result Address (Hexadecimal):</strong> `0x0414`</li>
    <li><strong>Status:</strong> <strong style="color: #16a34a;">PASSED ✅</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Test Case 2: 2D Column-Major Order Memory Calculation</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Base Address = `1000`, Element Size = `4` bytes, Rows = `4`, Cols = `4`, Target Row = `2`, Target Col = `3`, Indexing = `0-Based`.</li>
    <li><strong>Calculation:</strong> $\text{Offset} = [(3 - 0) \times 4 + (2 - 0)] \times 4 = [12 + 2] \times 4 = 14 \times 4 = 56$ bytes.</li>
    <li><strong>Result Address (Decimal):</strong> `1056`</li>
    <li><strong>Result Address (Hexadecimal):</strong> `0x0420`</li>
    <li><strong>Status:</strong> <strong style="color: #16a34a;">PASSED ✅</strong></li>
  </ul>

